Z||000006||Standard||07-16-2000||01:42 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Phil:<BR><B>OOPS!! A trifle large</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The wing or the exhaust tips?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P>Just kiddin' man!  Your car looks great!<P>------------------<BR>Mike -- Golden Valley, MN<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 147,000 miles and counting!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000007||86SE||07-17-2000||11:36 PM||||Update<P>Everything is now shot, the only things that stayed on the car was the top piece the surrounds the sunroof and windsheild, and the notchback clip piece.  I started piecing the car backtogether, started from the back, workin up to the front.  Everything is put on from the rear bumper to the door skins and mirrors.<P>I love the color, and I now know why Ferrari make only one yellow.<P>I kept the mirrors black, vents black, moldings black, all outer trimming black, and rocker panel covers black.  It looks great so far, I shot some pictures of it all tore up, shot some while it was all taped, and i'll shot some tomorrow when its finished.  Then i'll take some more pictures when the windows are all tinted up!<P>Overall the car looks excellent, best yellow i've seen, can be seen from miles away.<P>Oh yeah, I painted the gas filler piece (not the lid but the part the lid hinges to) black for the extra black touch, and I painted the center caps on the wheels yellow for the extra cool yellow touch!<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Fiero||||reg||14
